The rtranscribe R package is released under the MIT licence (see LICENSE
and LICENSE.md).

The package bundles third-party sources under src/transcribe-cpp/, which are
compiled into the package's shared object at install time. Every bundled
component is MIT licensed; there is no copyleft code in the compiled path.
Verbatim copies of the upstream notices are installed under inst/licenses/
and are available from an installed package with:

    system.file("licenses", package = "rtranscribe")

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Component        Licence   Copyright                        Notice
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
transcribe.cpp   MIT       (c) 2026 The transcribe.cpp      inst/licenses/
                           authors                          transcribe.cpp-LICENSE

ggml             MIT       (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors   inst/licenses/
(core + CPU                                                 ggml-LICENSE
 backend)

llamafile /      MIT       (c) 2024 Mozilla Foundation      header comment of
tinyBLAS                                                    src/transcribe-cpp/ggml/
(sgemm.cpp,                                                 src/ggml-cpu/llamafile/
 compiled in via                                            sgemm.cpp
 GGML_LLAMAFILE=ON)

miniz            MIT       (c) 2013-2014 RAD Game Tools     inst/licenses/
                           and Valve Software;              miniz-LICENSE
                           (c) 2010-2014 Rich Geldreich
                           and Tenacious Software LLC
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

Note on miniz: the amalgamated miniz.c / miniz.h files carry a header comment
describing the code as "public domain". That comment is a stale upstream
artifact. The authoritative licence for the bundled copy is the MIT text at
src/transcribe-cpp/src/third_party/miniz/LICENSE (reproduced in
inst/licenses/miniz-LICENSE), which is also what upstream's
THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md identifies as controlling.

Pruned components: the upstream ggml tree ships GPU backends (ggml-cuda,
ggml-vulkan, ggml-sycl, ggml-metal, ggml-openvino and others), some of which
contain Apache-2.0 licensed files. None of them are vendored into this
package and none are compiled -- tools/vendor.sh keeps only the CPU backend.

The exact upstream revision that was vendored is recorded in
src/transcribe-cpp/VENDOR.
